  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "Issue:\n\nPath points are in world-space. Importing a path in another world or in the same instance but in a different location causes it to spawn at the original world position of the recorded path.\n\nUsing local-space for the camera anchor partially solves the problem, but breaks if the original world origin the path was recorded in drastically differs from the current one.\n\nThis would make it easier to create path presets for montages across different worlds and locations.\n\nSuggestion:\n\nAllow users to spawn a path relative to their position, relative to a local marker, or something similar.",
